      "content": "that's a pretty intense way to frame it—calling them \"far-left\" and \"far-right\" makes it sound like it's just a political shouting match. isn't there more of a substantive economic argument involved? like, beyond just party lines, what are the actual core arguments people use to justify wanting to break them up vs wanting to leave them alone?",
